{#- The body of one detailed country entry on /europe/.

    Pulled out into an include because the three groups on that page — training
    routes, the countries people actually go to, and the short entries — print
    the same fields and must never drift apart. One template, one shape, and a
    missing field is missing everywhere rather than in one place nobody checks.

    Expects `c`, one entry from europe.json's `countries` array, from the
    enclosing for-loop. Nunjucks include inherits the caller's context.

    Several fields are either a plain string or an object of
    {status, text} — the object form is used wherever the honest answer is "we
    have not checked this". `{% if x.text %}` distinguishes them: a string has
    no `.text`. -#}

